{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c3688515-d8b2-43c3-8b08-0d33f33f59b6","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Now draw a median from each remaining vertex. All three medians meet at one point, called the centroid.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"medians","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"n","at":{"mid":["a","c"]},"label":"N"},{"kind":"point","id":"p","at":{"mid":["a","b"]},"label":"P"},{"kind":"segment","id":"bn","from":{"at":"b"},"to":{"at":"n"}},{"kind":"segment","id":"cp","from":{"at":"c"},"to":{"at":"p"}},{"kind":"point","id":"g","at":{"hit":["am","bn"]},"label":"G"}]},{"op":"text","id":"meeting","anchor":{"el":"midpoint","side":"below","gap":0.1},"content":"G is the centroid: all three medians meet."}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c3688515-d8b2-43c3-8b08-0d33f33f59b6","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The centroid also divides every median in a two-to-one ratio. The longer portion is always next to the vertex.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"ratio","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"measure","from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"g"},"label":"2 parts"},{"kind":"measure","from":{"at":"g"},"to":{"at":"m"},"label":"1 part"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"meeting","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"AG:GM=2:1\\qquad AG=\\frac{2}{3}AM"}],"checkpoint":null}}
